<Chapter id="changelog">
<h2>13. Document changelog</h2>
  <p>Revisions to this reference, newest first. Dates track when a finding was
  settled in the implementing client, not when the protocol itself changed. All
  entries describe the same target: SC2 <code>5.0.16.97563</code>, with native
  BSN metadata recovered from build <code>97364</code>.</p>

  <dl>
    <dt>2026-08-09 — Social graph</dt>
    <dd>Documented the whisper family (<code>Chat/19</code> send and receive,
    <code>Chat/30</code> echo, <code>Chat/20</code> mapped but not yet decoded),
    including the <code>PlayerTarget</code> choice that selects a whisper target by
    presence id, toon name, account id, or toon handle. Added the Battle.net group
    subsystem on <code>S2Mp</code>: <code>46</code> group list, <code>51</code>
    search, <code>53</code> member clan tags, <code>54</code> invitation action,
    and <code>55</code> group info. Added presence targeting on <code>Pres</code>
    (<code>2</code> statistics subscribe, <code>3</code> statistics update,
    <code>4</code> temporary presence) with the additional <code>Pres/0</code>
    field handles the client decodes, and the toon-resolution routes
    <code>Prfl/1</code>, <code>Prfl/3</code>, and <code>Frnd/6</code>. The runtime
    registry table and the unresolved list were brought in step with these
    routes.</dd>

    <dd>Corrected the client channel index: its wire range is 0&ndash;6, but the
    service grants at most six concurrent channels, so the seventh index exists
    without ever being handed out. Noted the <code>Chat/0</code> club locator's
    sixteen reserved bits ahead of the group id.</dd>

    <dt>2026-08-04 — Initial reference</dt>
    <dd>First published description: the BGS protobuf control plane and logon
    sequence, the Front-to-Sunken GameUtilities handoff, the native bit-packed BSN
    record stream and its embedded schema metadata, resume authentication and
    transport protection, the runtime service registry, and the core services
    &mdash; <code>Auth</code>, <code>Conn</code>, <code>Toon</code>,
    <code>Pres</code>, <code>Frnd</code>, <code>Cach</code>, <code>S2Ms</code>,
    <code>S2Mp</code>, <code>Prfl</code>, and <code>Chat</code> &mdash; covering
    channels, roster, and messages.</dd>
  </dl>
  <BackToContents />
</Chapter>
